{
  "schema": "outshine/mod/1",
  "name": "ardeche",
  "subject": "The relief reference point: the limestone rim of the Ardeche gorge, where a chunk cell is 13.66 m across and the surface leans about 20 degrees. A salt pan cannot show a height oracle that evaluates the wrong surface, because on a plane every interpolant agrees; a curved cell separates the drawn triangle from any bilinear filter over the same four heights, and it separates the two diagonals from each other \u2014 turning the diagonal moves the ground under the sixteen standpoints below by up to 0.23 m.",
